        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "c2cac405-7c6b-5b1e-96ae-212677b58c24",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Robert Case\n- Events: 1991 Perfect Storm, 1991 Halloween blizzard\n- Concepts: storm naming, low-pressure development, weather blocking, moisture transport\n\nFacts:\n- During the last week of October 1991, the 1991 Perfect Storm blocked most weather patterns over the eastern half of the United States.\n- During the last week of October 1991, the 1991 Perfect Storm caused moisture from the Gulf of Mexico to be funneled straight northward over the region affected by the 1991 Halloween blizzard.\n- On October 29, 1991, the initial area of low pressure for the 1991 Perfect Storm developed off Atlantic Canada.\n- Robert Case is best known for inspiring the naming of the 1991 Perfect Storm as \"The Perfect Storm.\"",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
